From: =?UTF-8?q?K=C3=A9vin=20R=C3=A9mondi=C3=A8re?= <kevin@localhost>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 16:15:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 25/57] vulkan: elide the GDN input-state GET_ROWS
 ([TAG_GDN_ZC] input side)

The GDN state gather (GET_ROWS on the recurrent ring, ~780 us/token on the 125B
decode profile) is pure plumbing: the kernel can read the ring row directly.

Same backend-fusion philosophy as the write side: a prepare pass detects, by
dependency, a GDN whose state input is a contiguous GET_ROWS(ring, I32 index)
walked back through RESHAPE/VIEW ops, with a single-entry index (single seq) and
single-token decode. The GET_ROWS node is skipped; the kernel reads the ring row
data_idx[seq] * state_row_stride and an extra binding carries the index vector.

Safety: restricted to n_seq_tokens == 1 && n_seqs == 1. The kernel writes only
ring row "head" (slot 0, n_written = 1); the read row is idx*mem_size + src0.
Either the rows differ, or they are the same row of the only sequence, in which
case every read/write of an element belongs to one workgroup which loads its
slice into registers before storing - no cross-workgroup hazard. The ring read
(and the index vector) are declared in the sync bookkeeping so prior writes
(rs_z zeroing, rollback CPY) still complete before the gather-free read.

Disabled under GGML_VULKAN_CHECK_RESULTS (the per-node checker would compare
against a never-computed gather) and under GGML_VK_DISABLE_GDN_CACHE_FUSION.

Shader: binding 8 (I32 indices), push constants use_fused_state/state_row_stride;
the legacy path binds a dummy and never reads them.

Tests: 5 new GATED_DELTA_NET_ZC cases reproduce the production gather pattern,
including the read-row == write-row aliasing case (K=1 and K=4) and a disjoint
rollback row. 11/11 ZC cases pass CPU vs Vulkan with both fusions active,
11/11 with fusion disabled, 36/36 legacy unchanged.
